Chapter Four: Adventures in Mine town

Galanda and Ellora continued to explore the mines together. Galanda
found two more potions in the current dungeon level. Curious, Galanda
drank one. It tasted disgusting, but Galanda suddenly felt restored to
her original strength! Encouraged, Galanda drank the other one, and
suddenly saw a vision of the all the items nearby. There weren't very
many. Galanda also decided to wear a blessed hard had that she had
come across, because she could still cast her spells well, and needed
the extra defence, particularly from falling rocks.

Galanda then lead Ellora down to the next dungeon level, and after a
brief walk was encountered by a strange brown bulging creature, which
tried to bite Galanda's boots! Galanda became angry but held back with
her mace. The mace may become more damaged, and Galanda could not
afford that. Galanda walked around collecting some daggers from some
dwarves that Ellora had been killing. Galanda walked up to the brown
creature, but stayed a square away from it and thew one of the
daggers. Galanda gasped as the brown bulged and split into two! Ellora
came running at the sight of more food, and started biting the new
one. Galanda threw daggers for a few turns at one, then it split
again, just as Ellora had killed one! Galanda threw down her daggers
and gave up, waiting for Ellora to kill and eat them both. Once Ellora
had finished eating, Galanda walked forward, exploring the last of the
cavern, finding a whistle and a spell book!

Galanda tried reading the spell book, and learnt the spell ‘haste
self', but realised that she was very poor at it. Galanda was
burdened, so left the book where she found it. Galanda walked to the
stair and blew her whistle, causing Ellora to come running.

Galanda and Ellora began exploring the next level of the mines,
Galanda exploring and taking things, Ellora doing most of the
fighting. Galanda found a look glass, but was trapped in a web while
taking it. She struggled against the web as a giant spider came up.
Galanda managed to escape the web and kill the spider, but was
burdened. After a bit of considering, she decided to leave behind the
mighty artefact until she had fully explored these caverns. Galanda
buried the blade into the web, and quickly walked on.

After much exploring, and constant checks to see that Trollsbane had
not been taken, Galanda gazed over her new possessions. She had found
another strange grey stone, seemingly identical to the first, an oil
lamp, a dark green potion, and a strange pair of jungle boots. Galanda
felt nothing wrong with the boots, so took of her old boots, and put
the jungle boots on. To her dismay, nothing interesting happened.
Galanda sighed, wishing she could find some magically enchanted boots
that would get her to the amulet of yendor faster! Galanda replaced
the jungle boots with her old boots, since they were large and
protected her feet better.

"Here girl!" called Galanda and blew her whistle to attract the dog's
attention. Galanda walked over to the spider web, and was glad to see
Trollsbane still hidden. She hefted it up, again feeling it's weight
slowing her down. Galanda began to haul it over to the stairs, when
the floor she was walking on gave way, and she suddenly found herself
in a deep pit. Cursing, Galanda attempted to hall herself, and her
equipment, out of the pit.

"Hey babe," came a strange deep voice from above. Galanda paused and
looked upwards. Just out of the pit was an Incubus! Galanda had heard
a lot about those!

"Get nicked!" yelled Galanda, very un-priestly. She didn't really
care. From outside the pit Galanda could hear Ellora barking in
disgust. The Incubus jumped into the pit, then took off Galanda's
helmet, feeling her soft hair.

"Take off your armour, let's get a little closer..." said the Incubus.
Galanda was completely disgusted, and slapped the Incubus.

"Your such a great girl... I wish..." said the dejected Incubus,
disappearing. Galanda put her helmet back on and climbed out of the
pit to continue down, but arrived a bit early than intended, when she
fell through another trap door. Thankfully Galanda landed near the
stairs up, and climbed back up to get Ellora.

Galanda blew hard on her whistle, then waited. Instead of Ellora, the
Incubus came running up.

"Hey, remember me babe?" asked the Incubus.

"Yeah," said Galanda, right before bashing the incubus with her mace.
Just as Galanda had finished repaying the Incubus, Ellora came running
up, and followed Galanda down the stairs.

The first thing Galanda could hear on the next level was another
shopkeeper, complaining about shopkeepers. She was amazed, who would
possibly put a shop out here? Galanda walked through a few small
rooms, then opened a door. She was even more amazed when she saw a
large town, filled with small homes, shops and even patrolling guards.
Galanda walked around, and saw not one, but four shops and a temple!
Unfortunately the temple was worshipping a different god, and Galanda
ignored it for the moment.

"Aaah! Damn dog!" came a cry from nearby. Galanda tore round the
corner and saw Ellora biting one of the guards, which was slashing at
Ellora in annoyance.

"ELLORA! Bad dog!" called Galanda, but Ellora continued to attack the
guard. Galanda ran up, and shoved Ellora into a small empty house,
then locked the door.

"That your dog? You ought to keep it in better control," said the
guard in an annoyed tone.

"Sorry, just let her get out of my sight," apologised Galanda, wishing
to herself she had a leash.

Galanda then continued to explore the town, and visit all of the
shops. The first store she looked in was a general store, and she
bought a scroll of identity, and a blessed potion of healing. She
tried to sell her grey stones, but the shopkeeper was not even
slightly interested in one of them, and offer a large price for the
second. Galanda ditched the worthless stone, and decided to use her
new scroll to identify the stone. To her great surprise the stone
turned out to be a luck stone! Galanda was willing to bet that it
would increase her luck more if it were blessed, so she wet it with
another one of her potions of holy water. Galanda then looked into the
lighting store. To her surprise, she saw another magic lamp, that was
already blessed! Unfortunately she didn't have enough gold to cover
the cost, so Galanda walked back to the general store and sold her
empty wands of fire and undead turning, her wand of secret door
detection, her jungle boots, and Trollsbane.

"I'LL GET WHAT!?" screeched Galanda when she heard the price for
Trollsbane.

"You heard me, twenty-five zorkmids, take it or leave it," repeated
the shopkeeper.

"This is a genuine artefact! You'll probably never see one of these
again!" yelled Galanda.

"Twenty-five, take it or leave it," said the shopkeeper again. Galanda
sighed in frustration.

"FINE!!" She yelled and stormed out of the shop, pushing past some
guards that had come to see what all the commotion was about. Galanda
rushed into the lighting store again to purchase the magic lamp.

"Slow down, think clearly," said the shopkeeper. Galanda dumped her
gold on the floor and walked out with the lamp, ignoring the
shopkeeper. Galanda next looked into the hardware store and looked
around. She saw a stethoscope, and purchased it to keep track of
Ellora's health. Galanda finally went into the food store, and saw a
large box. Upon opening it she was blasted by cold, and a foul stench
of corpses. What kind of disgusting shop was this? Galanda paused
before closing it, seeing the corpse of a cockatrice! She knew that a
cockatrice had magical powers of stone, and she wondered if the same
powers could be used from the corpse...

Galanda walked over to where she had left Ellora, and began to unlock
the door.

"Hey there! Stop picking that lock!" yelled one of the guards.

"But my dogs in there!" complained Galanda. Galanda decided to wait
until the guard was out of sight, but while she was waiting a werewolf
came up. Galanda drew her mace and began fighting the wolf, but before
she could kill it, the werewolf bit deep into Galanda's leg, and she
felt very feverish. Galanda quickly slew the wolf and panicked, if she
didn't do something she would become a werewolf herself! Galanda
racked her memory for what she had been taught.

"Wolfsbane!" cried out Galanda in realisation. She quickly searched
her pack for one of the sprigs of wolfsbane she had been carrying, and
ate it. Galanda felt the fever disappear and sighed in relief. She
then walked back over to where Ellora was, and unlocked the door now
that the guards were gone. Once Ellora saw Galanda she ran up eagerly.

Galanda locked the door to the room and took a look at her equipment.
First thing first, the magic lamp. Galanda took out the lamp, crossed
her fingers, and rubbed the lamp.

"How dare you disturb me!?" the djinn inside yelled. Galanda took out
her mace and attacked the djinn in annoyance. The djinn was easier to
kill now she was more experienced. Two magic lamps, two hostile
djinns! Luck is definitely not going my way, thought Galanda.* Galanda
looked over the rest of her items and decided to try out her two
unknown potions, and her unknown scroll. She drunk one potion, and
suddenly felt fully healed, though she was not far off anyway. She
drunk the second and suddenly felt more agile than before. Galanda was
glad at these, and read the scroll.

"Squeak!" came a voice from low down. Galanda felt a pain in her leg
and looked down. The scroll had somehow created a sewer rat! Galanda
killed it in one blow, and Ellora ate it hungrily. Galanda walked out
of the room with Ellora, headed for the general store again. About
half way there, she heard barking and yelling again, and saw Ellora
looking quite happy with herself, and a dead guard on the ground.
Galanda was shocked and kicked Ellora in anger. Ellora whined, and
came back up. Galanda decided to check the guards body (making sure no
one was watching) and took a studded leather armour, swapping it for
her own. Galanda walked to the general store, making sure Ellora was
in sight, and purchased another few scrolls of identify in case she
found anything of interest deeper in the caverns.

Galanda walked towards the stairs down, but was attacked by a red
Naga. Galanda swung her mace, thinking that it would be easy, when the
red Naga breathed fire! Galanda screamed in pain as the fire burned
her, and her gloves. Galanda quickly healed herself while Ellora
finished the Naga off. Galanda took another few steps and suddenly a
gush of water hit head, causing her helmet to rust! Grumbling in
annoyance, Galanda lit her lamp, and continued down further into the
caverns...
 
